targets.outcome_quote:
The ratings of likability and the quality of the interaction did not differ significantly, effect sizes were small and confidence intervals were large. The CASA theory was not supported by this experiment. Results—the effect size magnitude—of Nass et al. [
48
] were not replicated, although (1) sample size and thus statistical power was higher, and (2) social cues were expected to be stronger in robots compared to computers.
